  "notes": "Anglo-Eastern Plantations (AIM/Main Market UK, USD reporting). Operates ~120,000 ha (296.5k acres) of oil palm in Sumatra and Sabah/Bintulu. UK semi-annual reporter (H1 interim June + FY December). Revenue is CPO + palm kernel sales; segment split by Indonesia / Malaysia operations from annual report segment notes. AEP carries minimal debt; large net cash position from accumulated CPO cash flows. Hectares converted to thousand acres via x 2.47. Per-share dividend declared in pence-sterling at AGM (board uses GBp); reported here as USD per disclosure year. Coverage extended to FY 1995 from archived annual reports / Companies House filings; AEP transitioned from GBP to USD reporting in 2002 — pre-2002 figures restated to USD at average year exchange rate from disclosed IR archive. Plantation hectarage grew from ~26,000 ha (1995, ~64k acres) to ~120,000 ha (2024) via acquisitions and replanting; totalAcresK reflects disclosed snapshot. Pre-2010 only annual figures available; H1 cadence began consistently from 2010. Operating expense breakdown (Cost of sales / Administrative expenses / Other operating expenses) reconstructed from consolidated income statement Note 5 of annual reports filed on angloeastern.co.uk IR archive; H1 interims do not split opex categories so field omitted there.",
